# TLS terminator for the AWS deployment host.
#
# The app container is no longer published to the internet; it binds loopback
# only and this is the single public entrypoint. Caddy obtains and renews the
# Let's Encrypt certificate on its own (TLS-ALPN-01 on :443, HTTP-01 fallback on
# :80) and redirects plain HTTP to HTTPS.
#
# The hostname is interpolated from the container environment, so it lives in
# .env beside the other deployment values rather than in git. If DNS for
# $APP_DOMAIN does not point at this host, the ACME challenge fails and the
# deploy health gate fails with it — which is the point: a green deploy then
# means the domain really resolves here.
#
# `encode` is deliberately absent. Its response writer wraps the proxied stream
# and breaks Server-Sent Events (caddyserver/caddy#6293), which this app uses for
# streaming assistant responses. `reverse_proxy` alone flushes text/event-stream
# correctly. Add compression on the upstream, not here, if it is ever needed.

{$APP_DOMAIN} {
	reverse_proxy {$APP_UPSTREAM}
}
